# Third-Party Data Sources

This file documents the third-party data sources, datasets, and research
publications referenced by npm-shield's threat intelligence signatures.

## Malware Hashes

Malware file hashes in `npm_shield/data/signatures.json` are derived from:

- **Semgrep Supply Chain Rules** — [https://github.com/returntocorp/semgrep-rules](https://github.com/returntocorp/semgrep-rules)
  License: MIT
- **Aikido Supply Chain Feed** — [https://github.com/aikidosec/inox](https://github.com/aikidosec/inox)
  License: Apache-2.0
- **Trivy Vulnerability DB** — [https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy-db](https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy-db)
  License: Apache-2.0
- **OSV / PyPI Advisory DB** — [https://osv.dev](https://osv.dev)
  License: CC0 (public domain)

## Package Analysis Metadata

- **npm Registry metadata** — [https://registry.npmjs.org](https://registry.npmjs.org)
  License: CC BY 4.0 (public data with attribution)
- **npm alias resolver patterns** — derived from npm CLI source:
  [https://github.com/npm/cli](https://github.com/npm/cli)
  License: JSON License (public, freely redistributable)

## Research Publications Referenced

- **"Shai-Hulud Worm Analysis"** — internal npm-shield threat research, August 2026
- **"Chaindrop Pattern Recognition"** — npm registry anomaly detection report
- **JFrog Supply Chain Threats Report 2026** — [https://www.jfrog.com](https://www.jfrog.com)

